.TH VAULT 1 "November 2026" "Vault 1.0.0" "Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
vault \- Swiss army knife for hackers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvault\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
\fBvault\fR \fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR \fB\-info\fR
.PP
\fBvault\fR \fB\-ip\fR \fIIP\fR \fB\-sp\fR \fIPORT1\fR \fB\-ep\fR \fIPORT2\fR \fB\-t\fR \fIN\fR
.PP
\fBvault\fR \fB\-all\fR \fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR \fB\-exclude\fR \fISCANS\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBvault\fR is a Python 3 command\-line security scanner and penetration
testing toolkit: information gathering, web application scanning (XSS, LFI,
open redirects, CMS detection), network and port scanning, hash cracking and
various attacks.
.PP
Every invocation must select at least one action flag (e.g. \fB\-info\fR,
\fB\-ssl\fR or \fB\-xss\fR) or \fB\-all\fR. Running \fBvault\fR without an
action flag prints the help text and is a usage error (exit status 2).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS TARGET OPTIONS
.IP "\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR" 24
URL for scanning.
.IP "\fB\-ip\fR, \fB\-\-ip\fR \fIIP\fR" 24
IP address for port scanning.
.IP "\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR" 24
Single port for scanning (shorthand for \fB\-sp\fR/\fB\-ep\fR with the same
value).
.IP "\fB\-sp\fR, \fB\-\-start_port\fR and \fB\-ep\fR, \fB\-\-end_port\fR \fIPORT\fR" 24
Start and end port of the scan range.
.IP "\fB\-ip_start_range\fR, \fB\-ip_end_range\fR \fIIP\fR" 24
Start and end of the IP range to scan; both must be given together.
.IP "\fB\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR" 24
Directory to scan (used by \fB\-bruteforce\fR).
.IP "\fB\-target_bssid\fR \fIBSSID\fR" 24
Target BSSID (used with \fB\-deauth\fR).
.IP "\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interface\fR \fIIFACE\fR" 24
Networking interface to use.
.IP "\fB\-source_port\fR \fIPORT\fR" 24
Source port for sending packets.
.IP "\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dork\fR \fIQUERY\fR" 24
Perform Google dorking with the given query.
.SS SCAN MODES
.IP "\fB\-ssl\fR" 24
Perform an SSL scan.
.IP "\fB\-info\fR" 24
Gather information about the target.
.IP "\fB\-comment\fR, \fB\-email\fR" 24
Find HTML comments or email addresses.
.IP "\fB\-fuzz\fR" 24
Fuzz the target URL.
.IP "\fB\-xss\fR" 24
Scan for XSS vulnerabilities.
.IP "\fB\-this\fR" 24
Only scan the given URL, do not crawl.
.IP "\fB\-lfi\fR" 24
Scan for LFI vulnerabilities.
.IP "\fB\-detect_cms\fR" 24
Perform CMS detection.
.IP "\fB\-jquery\fR" 24
Check the jQuery version and get its vulnerabilities.
.IP "\fB\-admin\fR" 24
Find the admin panel on a given domain.
.IP "\fB\-orv\fR" 24
Test for open redirection vulnerability.
.IP "\fB\-honey\fR" 24
Detect a honeypot.
.IP "\fB\-whois\fR" 24
Perform a whois lookup of a given IP.
.IP "\fB\-ping_sweep\fR, \fB\-arp\fR" 24
ICMP echo sweep or ARP scan.
.IP "\fB\-fin\fR, \fB\-null\fR, \fB\-ack\fR, \fB\-xmas\fR" 24
Perform TCP FIN, NULL, ACK and XMAS scans (require root).
.IP "\fB\-os_scan\fR" 24
Perform an OS scan (requires the \fBnmap\fR(1) binary on \fBPATH\fR).
.IP "\fB\-cr\fR, \fB\-cri\fR" 24
Extract links or images from a web page.
.IP "\fB\-all\fR" 24
Run all scans that apply to the given target; requires \fB\-u\fR or
\fB\-ip\fR.
.IP "\fB\-exclude\fR \fISCANS\fR" 24
Comma\-separated scans to exclude when running \fB\-all\fR.
.IP "\fB\-hash\fR" 24
Start a hash scan.
.IP "\fB\-md5\fR, \fB\-sha1\fR, \fB\-sha224\fR, \fB\-sha256\fR, \fB\-sha512\fR" 24
Scan MD5, SHA1, SHA224, SHA256 and SHA512 hashes.
.SS ATTACKS
.IP "\fB\-ddos\fR" 24
Perform a DDoS attack.
.IP "\fB\-mac_flood\fR" 24
Perform a MAC flooding attack.
.IP "\fB\-arp_spoof\fR" 24
Perform ARP spoofing.
.IP "\fB\-ping_death\fR" 24
Perform a ping of death attack.
.IP "\fB\-deauth\fR" 24
Perform a de\-authentication attack (WiFi).
.IP "\fB\-bruteforce\fR" 24
Perform a brute force attack through Authorization headers.
.IP "\fB\-keylogger\fR" 24
Capture keystrokes and send them by email (requires accessibility
permission).
.IP "\fB\-interval\fR \fISECONDS\fR" 24
Interval time for sending packets.
.SS UTILITY
.IP "\fB\-change_mac\fR, \fB\-mac\fR \fIMAC\fR" 24
Change the MAC address to \fIMAC\fR.
.IP "\fB\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR, \fB\-username\fR \fIUSER\fR, \fB\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR" 24
SMTP host, login and password for \fB\-keylogger\fR.
.IP "\fB\-sender\fR \fIEMAIL\fR, \fB\-destination\fR \fIEMAIL\fR" 24
From and to addresses for \fB\-keylogger\fR emails.
.SS OUTPUT OPTIONS
.IP "\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR" 24
Output all data to \fIFILE\fR.
.IP "\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR \fIN\fR" 24
Number of threads to use.
.IP "\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR" 24
Show tracebacks on errors.
.IP "\fB\-\-debug\fR" 24
Enable debug output.
.SS GENERAL
.IP "\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR" 24
Show the help message and exit.
.IP "\fB\-\-version\fR" 24
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP "0" 4
Successful completion.
.IP "1" 4
Runtime error (failed scan, unreachable target, bad external service
response, and so on).
.IP "2" 4
Usage error (unknown option, missing action flag, invalid URL/IP/range,
\fB\-all\fR without a target).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI<repo>/log/vault\-error\-<timestamp>\-<pid>.log\fR
Per\-session error log, created lazily on the first error of a session.
Only ERROR\-level records are written; a session with no errors creates no
files. Contains a session header (time, pid, python, platform, cwd, argv)
followed by one block per error (time, code, feature, message, optional
hint and traceback).
.TP
\fI<repo>/log/vault\-error\-<timestamp>\-<pid>.jsonl\fR
Machine\-readable sidecar of the error log: one JSON object per line (a
session header object first, then one object per error). If the log
directory cannot be created, both files fall back to the system temporary
directory.
.TP
\fI<repo>/src/payloads/\fR
Data files (payload lists, wordlists) used by the scanners.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBVAULT_LOG_DIR\fR
Override the directory for the per\-session error logs (default:
\fI<repo>/log\fR).
.TP
\fBVAULT_NAME\fR, \fBVAULT_PREFIX\fR, \fBVAULT_PYTHON\fR
Launcher name, install directory and Python interpreter used by
\fIinstall.sh\fR (defaults: \fBvault\fR, \fI~/.local/bin\fR, the project's
conda environment).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBvault \-u http://example.com/ \-info\fR
Gather information about the site.
.TP
\fBvault \-u http://example.com/ \-xss \-this\fR
Scan only that page for XSS vulnerabilities, without crawling.
.TP
\fBvault \-ip 192.168.1.1 \-sp 1 \-ep 1000 \-t 50\fR
Port scan the target with 50 threads.
.TP
\fBvault \-all \-u http://example.com/ \-exclude ddos,keylogger\fR
Run every applicable scan except DDoS and the keylogger.
.TP
\fBvault \-hash \-md5 \-dir payloads/\fR
Scan MD5 hashes against the wordlist directory.
.TP
\fBvault \-ssl \-u example.com \-o ssl\-report.txt\fR
Run an SSL scan and write the results to a file.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README (\fIREADME.md\fR) and the Sphinx documentation in
\fIdocs/\fR.
.SH BUGS
Raw\-socket scans (\fB\-fin\fR, \fB\-null\fR, \fB\-ack\fR, \fB\-xmas\fR,
\fB\-os_scan\fR) and attacks (\fB\-ddos\fR, \fB\-mac_flood\fR,
\fB\-arp_spoof\fR, \fB\-ping_death\fR, \fB\-deauth\fR) require root and
often fail on macOS and in sandboxed environments.
.PP
Features backed by third\-party services (\fB\-ssl\fR via SSL Labs,
\fB\-honey\fR via Shodan, \fB\-d\fR via Google, \fB\-jquery\fR via a CVE
feed) are network\-dependent and can be rate\-limited or blocked. SSL Labs
rejects IP addresses and some hostnames. The keylogger
(\fB\-keylogger\fR) needs macOS Accessibility permission and will not run
unattended.
